## TODO: search-state-persistence

When a user opens a mod from the Browse page and navigates back (back arrow or ESC),
they are returned to the initial Browse page state instead of their previous search results.
Sort selection (e.g. "updated date") also resets on each visit.

Root cause: `BrowsePage` unmounts on tab switch (intentional, for fresh data), which discards
all local search/sort/scroll state. Fix would require lifting search state up to `App.tsx`
or preserving it with CSS-hidden approach (same as `InstalledPage` / `SettingsPage`).

Note: the fresh-fetch-on-visit behavior is desirable — only the search/sort *inputs* need
to survive navigation, not the results themselves.

---

## TODO: zip-archive-detection

Some mods on modworkshop upload a .zip archive as their download file. The mod manager
downloads it, renames it to .pak, and places it in the mods folder — but the game ignores it
because it is not a real pak. The SHA256 in mod-index.db is computed on the zip, not the
extracted pak inside it, so identification fails silently.

Fix: in `install_mod_from_path` (mods.rs), read the first 4 bytes of the temp file before
installing. If they match the zip magic (`50 4B 03 04`), return an error immediately.
Surface it in the UI with a message explaining that the mod uses an archive format and must
be installed manually (extract the .pak and drop it into the mods folder).

Confirmed reproduction: "Real Weapon Names" mod — zip contains two .pak choices; user must
extract and place one manually.

